n the mirror, `_optional_union_locals` 12x vs 0x, `_string_char_iter` 2x vs 0x. AND `git log -S` OVER THE MIRROR FILE RETURNS ZERO COMMITS for both symbols — they have NEVER been in the mirror, in any commit; the live emitter gained them at `ce71e3ab`/`41a12274`/`b6c417f6`/`2336cc72`/`50caedae`/`856f0cdb`. Re-running the plane at each of the last fourteen commits gives `rc=1 diverged=2` at every one, so this is neither mine nor the previous window's. WHY THIS IS NOT A LINT: L1 is one of the THREE DISJOINT ORACLE PLANES the entire campaign rests on, and its whole job is to make "the mirror method we proved is the emitter method that runs" CHECKABLE rather than assertable. While it is red for a method, the whole-file proof of that mirror certifies a body THE EMITTER DOES NOT HAVE — route #51's finding one level down, at the SOURCE rather than the emission, where no byte-diff can ever see it. `w49d_expressions` IS PROVING THAT EXACT FILE RIGHT NOW; whatever verdict it returns does not cover the two missing branches. AND THE REASON NOBODY SAW EITHER: both planes are DRIVER-RUN. The runner gates on `doc-coherency` and IR conformance only. That is the campaign's own sentence — a signal nobody collects is not a signal — paid for a FOURTH time, and this time it was an L-plane. The previous windows' "both fidelity planes byte-identical" is a DIFFERENT measurement (byte-diffing two emissions across a change) and cannot see a mirror body that was never faithful in the first place. Recorded in full: getting-better/open-routes/finding-L1-fidelity-plane-red-at-head.md
