array had a known length") repaired `_array_coerce_arg`'s `stripped == "0"` case to
`(any (array int))` and left the function's TAIL — "Anything else (BinOp result,
parenthesised int expression) — coerce to placeholder since we can't recover the
array" — still answering `(Array.make 1 0)`, an array whose length the model KNOWS
to be 1. A string literal reaches that tail because it is neither `"0"`, nor
array-shaped, nor alphanumeric-after-stripping (the quotes).

SPELLINGS MEASURED, because the repair's blast radius depends on them:
