THE REFUSAL-COVERAGE GATE WAS MEASURING ITS OWN ARTIFACT
================================================================================
`check-refusal-witness-coverage.py` reported 85 of 198 compiler refusals DEMONSTRATED and
113 with no witness, and the handoff's queue item 5 priced the remaining 113 at "about five
minutes each". I started paying that price, wrote four witnesses — and three of them were
for refusals THE CORPUS ALREADY WITNESSED.

HOW THE GATE MATCHES. Each raise site contributes a FRAGMENT: the longest string literal in
its message, first 60 characters. A site counts as demonstrated when that fragment appears
in some censused refusal message. `bin/refusal-witness-census.tsv` holds those messages.

WHAT THE CENSUS ACTUALLY HELD. 318 of its 437 refusal rows were exactly 110 characters
long. The census writer truncates at 400; the committed artifact was generated by an older
writer that cut at 110, and nobody re-derived it. Fragments that begin after character 110
of a message could therefore NEVER match, no matter how many witnesses were written:

  0284 / 0285 fire PYCSL-SEM-CLASSINV. Their stored message ends
    "...Class invariants should only reference sel"
  while the site's fragment is
    "Class invariants should only reference self.field or constants."

Same for PYCSL-SEM-QUANTBINDER (witnessed by 0556/0674) and PYCSL-SEM-GHOSTSTR (witnessed
by 0304, whose row stops nine characters before the word the fragment needs).

>>> A COVERAGE GATE CAN BE MEASURING ITS OWN ARTIFACT RATHER THAN THE WORLD. Before paying
>>> the cost a gap implies, CHECK THAT THE GAP IS IN THE SUBJECT AND NOT IN THE INSTRUMENT
>>> — and the giveaway here was free: 318 rows sharing one exact length is not what real
>>> messages look like.

>>> AND THE ARTIFACT WAS ARGUING FOR WORK. "113 refusals need witnesses, five minutes each"
>>> is nine hours of corpus files, a third of which would have witnessed nothing and
>>> inflated both the corpus and the coverage number at once. A number that recommends
>>> effort deserves the same scrutiny as a number that reports success.

THE REPAIR, in three passes, each one refusing to overwrite a row it could not prove was
the same refusal: pass 1 rewrote a row only when the fresh message STARTS WITH the stored
