ROUTE #215, AND THE SIXTH ARTIFACT IN THE SAME INSTRUMENT
================================================================================
The advice audit found it. Auditing monomorphize's GT4 advice ("the recursive call must
use a concrete type") produced a file that would not verify, so I isolated with controls:
a generic CLASS verifies, a NON-generic function verifies, a generic FUNCTION does not.
The emission said why — `ident[int](3)` lowered to `(any int)`.

Probing that erasure produced the route:

    def ident[T](n: int) -> int:  return n          #@ ensures \result == n
    def probe() -> int:                             #@ ensures \result == 0
        a = ident[int](1); x = a; a = ident[int](2); return x - a

PROVED. The emission is `a := (any int); x := pycsl_erased_a; a := (any int);
(!x - pycsl_erased_a)` — the per-NAME erased constant is not refreshed on REBINDING, so
two different calls collapse to one value. The TRUE twin is REFUSED.

AND THE GROUND TRUTH IS SHARPER THAN I FIRST WROTE. `ident[int](1)` is NOT VALID PYTHON:
PEP 695 makes a generic CLASS subscriptable (`Box[int]()` runs) but a generic FUNCTION is
not — CPython 3.14 raises `TypeError: 'function' object is not subscriptable`. So the model
was proving a postcondition about a program that CANNOT RUN AT ALL.

>>> I ALMOST WROTE "CPYTHON ANSWERS -1". Running the carrier is what caught it: CPython
>>> RAISES. The route is realer than the version I nearly recorded, and the difference was
>>> one command.

REFUSED at `_run_pipeline` (a `\trusted` mirror twin, so no marker and no re-proof).
Blast radius measured first: 2 occurrences in the corpus (both in witness 1783), ZERO in
the mirror, the live tree and pycsl_lib. Witness 1796, control 1797.

TWO PLACEMENT MISTAKES, each caught by a control rather than by reading:
  * the scan used the stdlib `ast` while the pipeline parses with `frontend.pure_ast`, so
    it matched NOTHING — the exact wrong-node-family error route #209 was made of;
  * landed before Module 5 it fired BEFORE the TY3 checks and made GT4 DEAD, because GT4
    keys on a recursive call whose type ARGUMENT is the generic's own TypeVar and only the
    subscripted spelling expresses that. Witness 1783 stopped witnessing GT4, which is how
